                    {
                        "form_id": "706a2a14-d2fc-4c5e-9ec8-19197c6f4be3",
                        "entry_id": "2a7ada55-8a23-32fe-b6c6-c1f57e17b327",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "кутежа́х"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c4e3a6b5-07e8-3d39-9135-34d7306fcb88",
                        "entry_id": "2a7ada55-8a23-32fe-b6c6-c1f57e17b327",
                        "glosses": [
                            "действие по значению гл. кутить; шумная, разгульная попойка"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a50c91d-ef0b-4172-948d-22d5da2113db",
                                "sense_id": "c4e3a6b5-07e8-3d39-9135-34d7306fcb88",
                                "text": "Несмотря на то, что под влиянием Дмитрия я ещё не предавался обыкновенным студенческим удовольствиям, называемым кутежами, мне случилось уже в эту зиму раз участвовать в таком увеселении, и я вынес из него не совсем приятное чувство."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ee575e07-49d6-4c6b-9f7f-003123bb2012",
                                "sense_id": "c4e3a6b5-07e8-3d39-9135-34d7306fcb88",
                                "text": "Кутёж у полкового командира продолжался долго. Пили очень много."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d87e29b9-a6a7-4eca-9716-2f94d7f98216",
                                "sense_id": "c4e3a6b5-07e8-3d39-9135-34d7306fcb88",
                                "text": "Шумного разгула и кутежей, которые тогда были в моде, дядя бегал: оргии ему были противны, но он платил дань своему веку страшною влюбчивостью, не знавшею у него никакой меры и границ."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "29abd5dd-de5f-4906-b4b8-d3766291810e",
                        "source_entry_id": "2a7ada55-8a23-32fe-b6c6-c1f57e17b327",
                        "source_sense_id": "c4e3a6b5-07e8-3d39-9135-34d7306fcb88",
                        "target_lang_word": "binge",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "binge",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "107c607c-c324-3116-ac33-f6d48fbc58a8",
                                        "entry_id": "0fe39510-66b0-3e04-b8ec-7100ca41ca1e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A short period of excessive consumption, especially of food, alcohol, narcotics, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e6ae651b-5840-39af-940c-8ac9a45d17d9",
                                        "entry_id": "0fe39510-66b0-3e04-b8ec-7100ca41ca1e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A compressed period of an activity done in excess, such as watching a television show."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "binge",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "96949c03-8285-3bf1-a8cc-3d801f92d34a",
                                        "entry_id": "641abe09-f74b-305a-b104-a16508a70232",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To engage in a short period of excessive consumption, especially of excessive alcohol or media consumption."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "often",
                                            "transitive",
                                            "with-on"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "feca0577-d7ab-4946-aed8-81ffdf018647",
                                                "sense_id": "96949c03-8285-3bf1-a8cc-3d801f92d34a",
                                                "text": "I binged on ice cream."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e311673b-8039-4a3b-80ca-121598ca7067",
                                                "sense_id": "96949c03-8285-3bf1-a8cc-3d801f92d34a",
                                                "text": "She'll binge an entire series on the weekend."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "60c7fc65-35ca-461c-b92b-45f194342c13",
                                                "sense_id": "96949c03-8285-3bf1-a8cc-3d801f92d34a",
                                                "text": "I'm totally happy to binge when I'm not busy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a77524c4-a9e6-45d6-9d78-b68e1d95f963",
                                                "sense_id": "96949c03-8285-3bf1-a8cc-3d801f92d34a",
                                                "text": "It’s nice to think that our bubble baths and personal time might have a larger political purpose (“Um, Foucault! I’m not just bingeing Netflix – I’m engaging in Platonic political philosophy in order to better serve others!”), but more often than not, our acts of self-care are simply acts of privilege."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32cfcd10-e86c-437a-98ab-8938e644ec33",
                                                "sense_id": "96949c03-8285-3bf1-a8cc-3d801f92d34a",
                                                "text": "([Jesse] Armstrong, by his own admission, binged episodes of the All-In podcast, which features prominent investors and Trump’s AI/crypto czar David Sacks.)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "113f7b45-ccf0-4bd0-b396-247e7d1ded67",
                        "source_entry_id": "2a7ada55-8a23-32fe-b6c6-c1f57e17b327",
                        "source_sense_id": "c4e3a6b5-07e8-3d39-9135-34d7306fcb88",
                        "target_lang_word": "carouse",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "carouse",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "54f9dc79-e176-3ec9-afaf-363d24ae1e49",
                                        "entry_id": "f165a10c-d425-3fa3-b516-7323b3016b2d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To engage in a noisy or drunken social gathering."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b9f28e4-116a-4c14-8f74-5863f8dc80fe",
                                                "sense_id": "54f9dc79-e176-3ec9-afaf-363d24ae1e49",
                                                "text": "We are all going to carouse at Brian's tonight."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b999c5e-99b9-42d3-8bc9-3ae09ca623ae",
                                                "sense_id": "54f9dc79-e176-3ec9-afaf-363d24ae1e49",
                                                "text": "The prospect of two hundred (or more) loitering and carousing patrons streaming out of the club at 1 a.m. is profoundly disturbing to us."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "305c7533-d92f-3b84-a6a9-a952a83dab40",
                                        "entry_id": "f165a10c-d425-3fa3-b516-7323b3016b2d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To drink to excess."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be848210-a461-468f-afb5-11cf6d696c55",
                                                "sense_id": "305c7533-d92f-3b84-a6a9-a952a83dab40",
                                                "text": "If I survive this headache, I promise no more carousing at Brian’s."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "417b1f28-2c7e-4c7e-9fac-197c80beb7e6",
                                                "sense_id": "305c7533-d92f-3b84-a6a9-a952a83dab40",
                                                "text": "[…] the cup-bearers did fill great gems made in form of cups with ancient wine, and the Demons caroused to Lord Juss deep draughts in honour of this day of his nativity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "carouse",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3e71407b-d74b-3534-9610-da7bce412a5c",
                                        "entry_id": "36b0287b-ad2a-3771-875c-6ca3bed0e2d6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large draught of liquor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2bd9547b-8b76-486b-9b40-812fa24379c7",
                                                "sense_id": "3e71407b-d74b-3534-9610-da7bce412a5c",
                                                "text": "[…] therefore forward I went with my hey-de-gaies to Ilford, where I againe reſted, and was by the people of the towne and countrey there-about very very wel welcomed, being offred carowſes in the great ſpoon, one whole draught being able at that time to haue drawne my little wit drye; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e874e851-40bb-497b-bade-cba83f586477",
                                                "sense_id": "3e71407b-d74b-3534-9610-da7bce412a5c",
                                                "text": "Had our great Pallace the capacity\nTo Campe this hoaſt, we all would ſup together,\nAnd drinke Carowſes to the next dayes Fate […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1f4334f-e303-4efe-9bc1-624153ce4e27",
                                                "sense_id": "3e71407b-d74b-3534-9610-da7bce412a5c",
                                                "text": "[…] he hadde ſo many eyes watching ouer him, as he coulde not drinke a full Carouſe of Sacke, but the State was aduertised thereof, within few houres after."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c010ecd2-93a1-3611-81e0-f180f936840e",
                                        "entry_id": "36b0287b-ad2a-3771-875c-6ca3bed0e2d6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A drinking bout; a carousal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78eb115d-59e4-433d-9610-4c9364c96de5",
                                                "sense_id": "c010ecd2-93a1-3611-81e0-f180f936840e",
                                                "text": "The early feast and late carouse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c29e7fcf-a58d-4d70-95c9-06f05951a745",
                                                "sense_id": "c010ecd2-93a1-3611-81e0-f180f936840e",
                                                "text": "PORSON […] would not only frequently “steal a few hours from the night,” but see out both lights and liquids, and seem none the worse for the carouse."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f0c18bb1-ec83-425e-8c43-55b3c8e0d180",
                        "source_entry_id": "2a7ada55-8a23-32fe-b6c6-c1f57e17b327",
                        "source_sense_id": "c4e3a6b5-07e8-3d39-9135-34d7306fcb88",
                        "target_lang_word": "carousal",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "carousal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3d386504-227f-3f92-b187-80862e9c6d9e",
                                        "entry_id": "7d324af7-4202-3370-b9d8-04a62dbad172",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A noisy feast or social gathering, often with much alcohol consumption."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b7ff5f9-fa91-4bcd-9dff-49a6c07877f3",
                                                "sense_id": "3d386504-227f-3f92-b187-80862e9c6d9e",
                                                "text": "When Alcohol ursurps the throne, and Sober Rationality is ejected, every other consideration is lost; that of having a regular ‘spree’ alone prevails:—the excited passions proclaim for a grand carousal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab3de1c7-e993-4114-9b82-43974029fe0e",
                                                "sense_id": "3d386504-227f-3f92-b187-80862e9c6d9e",
                                                "text": "The earth-spirit of Tema, who loved carousals, heard from afar the songs and laughter of the people on Nassau."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "56f59602-8f47-453b-bab9-12c219dac72c",
                        "source_entry_id": "2a7ada55-8a23-32fe-b6c6-c1f57e17b327",
                        "source_sense_id": "c4e3a6b5-07e8-3d39-9135-34d7306fcb88",
                        "target_lang_word": "revel",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "revel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "23672e3a-dc96-3f6e-a7eb-843af71e680e",
                                        "entry_id": "1e19154e-b3ab-3958-9a79-cf332e27e474",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An instance of merrymaking; a celebration."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58cce071-2895-435c-b384-4c84fe88dbed",
                                                "sense_id": "23672e3a-dc96-3f6e-a7eb-843af71e680e",
                                                "text": "Our revels now are ended."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aca18dff-f948-49bd-af17-e0c2442463e7",
                                                "sense_id": "23672e3a-dc96-3f6e-a7eb-843af71e680e",
                                                "text": "\"I ought to arise and go forth with timbrels and with dances; but, do you know, I am not inclined to revels? There has been a little—just a very little bit too much festivity so far …. Not that I don't adore dinners and gossip and dances; not that I do not love to pervade bright and glittering places.[…]\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6af6bed5-7636-37af-9bc4-b1376e66528d",
                                        "entry_id": "1e19154e-b3ab-3958-9a79-cf332e27e474",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A kind of dance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2f542da9-4955-302d-a562-2a08f0922c04",
                                        "entry_id": "1e19154e-b3ab-3958-9a79-cf332e27e474",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A wake for the dead."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "revel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f81599c-977d-3f72-9b3d-f0cf9f497fd9",
                                        "entry_id": "2292a1cf-b76f-33fe-8572-481751cacb74",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make merry; to have a happy, lively time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bfcfa904-f6e0-4616-8dad-43eb209ee6bb",
                                                "sense_id": "4f81599c-977d-3f72-9b3d-f0cf9f497fd9",
                                                "text": "If there bee any lasie fellow, any that cannot away with worke, any that would wallow in pleasures, hee is hastie to be priested. And when hee is made one, and has gotten a benefice, he consorts with his neighbour priests, who are altogether given to pleasures; and then both hee, and they, live, not like Christians, but like epicures; drinking, eating, feasting, and revelling, till the cow come home, as the saying is."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3c80d12-2d11-421b-84ee-1dd32fc6d7f9",
                                                "sense_id": "4f81599c-977d-3f72-9b3d-f0cf9f497fd9",
                                                "text": "[…] so they might spend the livelong day as befitteth high holiday, in pleasure and action without care, and thereafter revel in the lofty presence chamber till night grew old with eating and drinking and all delight."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6372a7bb-20ef-3f07-83f9-877fd3ff3312",
                                        "entry_id": "2292a1cf-b76f-33fe-8572-481751cacb74",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To take delight (in something)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9a3e4f2-f7d4-4cdf-ad19-b8b7a0ba91e6",
                                                "sense_id": "6372a7bb-20ef-3f07-83f9-877fd3ff3312",
                                                "text": "Slowing down doesn't have to feel like holding back. It can be an opportunity to revel in sounds and sensations, to not be so concerned about where we are going but to enjoy the moment and become comfortable where we are."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "revel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "08e7e1a6-4e19-36c8-9edc-5d924dabd71f",
                                        "entry_id": "640a7943-afe4-3017-885b-103465c0ea7b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To draw back; to retract."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d8c386c-326c-432a-b4db-c4a32a1793a4",
                                                "sense_id": "08e7e1a6-4e19-36c8-9edc-5d924dabd71f",
                                                "text": "It then revelleth and drawethe backe agayne those humors which concurre towardes the Eyes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
